  "summary": {
    "en": "Journalist Tomás Beltrán was murdered outside his home and two local election candidates were shot dead in El Oro, while a priest died when a crucifix fell during mass, showing attacks on public figures in Ecuador. An Ecuadorian thief pleaded guilty to participation in the largest U.S. jewelry heist, linking Ecuadorian crime to transnational theft. A major Ecuadorian cocaine and weapons trafficking ring was busted in New York, indicating the reach of Ecuadorian criminal networks beyond the country. The UCDP recorded 2 battle-related deaths in 2019, according to UCDP.",
